cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below (see also the Research Use and Reproducibility section of the README: please record the commit ID and any arithmetic settings that affect results)."
type: software
title: "total-arith-hardware: total arithmetic down to logic gates and SystemVerilog"
authors:
  - name: "PureTearsDropped"
version: v1.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
license: 0BSD
repository-code: "https://github.com/PureTearsDropped/total-arith-hardware"
abstract: "Total arithmetic lowered to AND/OR/NOT/XOR gate graphs with automatic SystemVerilog generation (the emitted RTL is the traced gate graph of the audited Python golden), block floating point, (U,V,W) bilinear units, series evaluation, a gate-level pseudo-inverse solver, and elementary functions (exp/expm1/log/sqrt/rsqrt) as range reduction + Remez coefficient tapes with one-sided exits, exhaustively swept at float32. Verified with iverilog+cocotb against the golden models."
keywords:
  - "total arithmetic"
  - "FPGA"
  - "SystemVerilog"
  - "logic gates"
  - "signed digit arithmetic"
  - "hardware verification"
  - "elementary functions"
  - "Remez"
